								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=1384.msg20981#msg20981"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=1384.msg20981#msg20981">Re: Stigmas of Governement aid mixed with racism...makes me so angry...</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> March 16, 2007, 10:14:40 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">When my wife and I were dating we both had to use ebt cards.&nbsp; I was embarassed enough to use the card let alone figure out all the products I could and couldn&#039;t buy.&nbsp; I&#039;ve worked so many customer service jobs and I understand what its like to stand for 8 hours and have people berate you all day... but damn.&nbsp; That&#039;s why I try to go that extra mile a be nice to people when I&#039;m at the grocery store or a shop in general.&nbsp; Sometimes I see how shocked people are when I just tell them to &quot;take it easy&quot; or say &quot;thank you.&quot;&nbsp; <br /><br />I&#039;ve been there... long ass day, the lines don&#039;t stop, people complaining/bitching and somebody basically messes up the flow.&nbsp; You realize the people behind them are gonna get pissed and then take it all out on you.&nbsp; (because you took the time to actually give someone customer service.)&nbsp; But what that woman did wasn&#039;t cool... THAT WASN&#039;T EVEN HER LANE AND THAT WAS BEYOND RUDE.<br /><br />I&#039;m proud you said something; because most people wouldn&#039;t have and they&#039;d probably just go home and say,&quot;This guy kept fucking up in line and that cashier just stood there.&quot;<br /><br />I remember one time I held up the line because the card reader or my debt card wern&#039;t working right.&nbsp; The lady next in line gave me this dirty look and I just said &quot;Hey, I&#039;m sorry everybody my cards messing up or something.&quot;&nbsp; I finally got my shit straight and she was even more pissed off, &quot;GET A NEW FUCKING CARD, JESUS CHRIST!!!!&quot;&nbsp; I just politely smiled and was like &quot;peace.&quot;&nbsp; Damn... even saying sorry doesn&#039;t mean anything because I took an extra minute in line.<br /><br />I guess it&#039;s just the state of people in this go, go, go society.</div>
