							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">since the topic veered this way...<br /><br />I was listening to the radio the other day and they said, in the US, that 20% of total fossil fule consumption goes into food production. That&#039;s even higher than transportation, which makes up 18% of fossil fule consumption. Producing firtilizer and moving the food are very wasteful of fossil fues. So buying organic and locally grown food actually helps cut down on global warming.<br /><br />just a little factoid I wanted to share</div>
