								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=1384.msg21210#msg21210">Re: Stigmas of Governement aid mixed with racism...makes me so angry...</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #13 on:</b> March 17, 2007, 07:55:37 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">Interesting story I mustve completely spaced on earlier<br /><br />One time when I was 11 years old I was at Fred Meyers on Casino trying to buy some grub with food stamps... The cashier told me I couldnt use them and then I was subsequently ridiculed by some older ladies in the line for being white trash and things like that...Not to sound sappy though lol but my fam was dirt poor and I was pretty hungry that day so I got shitted on and had to walk it to the 7-11, thank goodness those guys didnt shit on me <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/smiley.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /> Back to the store though... I hadn&#039;t quite grown into my rebellious stage at that point so I just walked off like a dog with it&#039;s tail between its legs... However the the disrespect stuck with me and I can proudly say 2 times now a kid has been in my situation where people have tried to disrespect him for using EBT and I tore them to shreds.  Once it was an early 30&#039;s Lynnwood leather type cat ( grew up in evt/moved to lynnwood and thinks he is upper crust now) and the other time was a woman who was in her mid fifties.  Ironically enough both times it was at the same store, the Cost Cutter on Evergreen and Evt Mall Way.  Same exact situation happened to my brother when he was a kid at the 128th St. Albertsons.  Good for you though for sticking up for him.  <br /><br />Does a lifestyle Safeway have the hardwoods and the open nutritional lobby?  Believe it or not but the nicest Safeway Ive ever delivered to was in Marysville, people-wise and the general cleanliness of the store</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
